'Subject: bridgeline workorder\nfyi .\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by brenda f herod / hou / ect on 04 / 26 / 2000\n11 : 31 am - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nbrian heinrich\n04 / 25 / 2000 05 : 49 pm\nto : brenda f herod / hou / ect @ ect , mary solmonson / hou / ect @ ect\ncc : lisa b cousino / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : bridgeline workorder\ni have some information on the e - workorders ( ehurr and ehset ) that were set\nup to track the costs of bridgeline . apparently the workorders themselves\nwere not set up correctly so no costs could be coded to them in msa . we have\ncorrected the workorder set - ups and they should be working now . as for prior\ncosts , i think we will be able to get a list of all the payroll costs that we\nattempted to code to ehurr and ehset , and then book an entry in april that\nwould reclass them to the workorders . we would then be able to see all the\ncosts associated with the project , as you wanted to do from the beginning ,\nand code any future costs directly to the workorders . i will let you know\nmore when i finalize that this can really be done , i just wanted to keep you\nupdated on the progress .\nif you have any questions , please let me know .\nthanks ,\nbrian',ham
