'Subject: re : teco gas processing company\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by george weissman / hou / ect on 03 / 28 / 2000\n03 : 31 pm - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nmary m smith\n04 / 26 / 99 04 : 53 pm\nto : hank eisenhour\ncc : george weissman / hou / ect @ ect , eric wardle / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : re : teco gas processing company\nis there still a problem with this ? we need hplc to nominate for 1 / 99\nforward at meter no . 6884 . please let me know the status . thanks , mary\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by mary m smith / hou / ect on 04 / 26 / 99 04 : 49 pm\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\ngregory allen jackson\n04 / 26 / 99 02 : 22 pm\nto : hank eisenhour / hou / ect @ ect\ncc : mary m smith / hou / ect @ ect , george weissman / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : re : teco gas processing company\ni \' m not sure what \' s going on , but i did not see a teco deal ticket in mops\nfor houston pipeline company anywhere ( january 1999 to march 1999 ) . i did\nsee one on houston pipeline company resources .\nas my original note stated , i think this is a buy / sell which means that teco\ngas processing should appear in both the market and supply depending on\nhplc \' s position .\nplease let me know something asap .\n3 - 9768\nmary m smith\n04 / 12 / 99 12 : 39 pm\nto : george weissman / hou / ect @ ect , hank eisenhour\ncc : gregory allen jackson / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : teco gas processing company\nthe sitara deal needs to reflect 3 / 99 forward . 1 / 99 and 2 / 99 was done .\nthanks , mary\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by mary m smith / hou / ect on 04 / 12 / 99 12 : 37 pm\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\ngregory allen jackson\n04 / 12 / 99 09 : 44 am\nto : jennifer meador / hou / ect @ ect\ncc : mary m smith / hou / ect @ ect , theresa r kotrla / hou / ect @ ect , gary w\nlamphier / hou / ect @ ect , sabrae zajac / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : teco gas processing company\nmary , this is the message i left a voice mail concerning . in addition to the\nother producer at this meter , the following needs to be setup :\npops hplc transport delivery 12 - 41500 - 203 done ( there )\nmops hplc sale to teco gp 12 - 86978 - 101 needed ( think this is buy / sell\narrangement ) ; no deal ticket .\ngary lamphier is looking into the exxon jack creek receipt flow at meter 6884\n- make final determination on whether it \' s either hplr or hplc . the deal\nsetup in pops and mops as hplr .\nsummary :\nneed hplc sale to teco related to transportation delivery in pops .\nfinal determination on whether the current hplr purchase from teco at exxon\njack creek is correct or should hplc be purchasing from teco - starting in\nfebruary 1999 business .\nthanks for you help , 3 - 9768\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by gregory allen jackson / hou / ect on 04 / 12 / 99\n09 : 18 am - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nenron capital & trade resources corp .\nfrom : george weissman 04 / 09 / 99 04 : 22 pm\nto : gregory allen jackson / hou / ect @ ect\ncc : greg brazaitis / hou / ect @ ect , jim coffey / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : teco gas processing company\nre the teco contract at 6884 ( 2 / 24 / 99 ) :\nto : george weissman / hou / ect @ ect , mary jo johnson / hou / ect @ ect , cynthia\nhakemack / hou / ect @ ect , nidia a martinez / hou / ect @ ect , alexia\ngonzales / hou / ect @ ect , sean j smith / hou / ect @ ect , vance l taylor / hou / ect @ ect\ncc : melissa graves / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : gt # : 1917 - teco gas processing co . and houston pipe line company\ni am forwarding a copy of the committed reserves agreement ( first purchaser )\ncontract for your information . contract date : 12 / 01 / 98 , global number :\n96019500 , and synergi number : 012 - 86978 - 101 .\nplease give me a call if you have any questions .\nthanks ,\ndaniel\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by george weissman / hou / ect on 04 / 09 / 99 04 : 16 pm\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nenron capital & trade resources corp .\nfrom : george weissman 01 / 27 / 99 06 : 01 pm\nto : vance l taylor / hou / ect @ ect\ncc : melissa graves / hou / ect @ ect , ann elizabeth white / hou / ect @ ect , jim\ncoffey / hou / ect @ ect , greg brazaitis / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : teco gas processing company\nmelissa \' s second sentence refers to the teco gas processing company 12 / 1 / 98\ncontract covering meters 6884 and 419 . this contract was obtained in\nconnection with the seven oaks / turpentine lease line renewal , and it doesn \' t\nappear to have hit the system . please ensure that the contract is set up and\nfiled .\ngeorge\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - forwarded by george weissman / hou / ect on 01 / 27 / 99 05 : 47\npm - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nenron capital & trade resources corp .\nfrom : melissa graves 01 / 24 / 99 04 : 03 pm\nto : george weissman / hou / ect @ ect\ncc : amelia alland / hou / ect @ ect , daniel verastegui / hou / ect @ ect\nsubject : swift energy company , meter 2630 , 012 - 86150 - 103\ngeorge ,\nat the 9 th workday meeting you had asked if we had seen the paper on the\nabove referenced . i have checked our database , and it appears that we have\nnot . the contract in the system does reflect at gs at this point .\ni also checked on teco gas processing company , and it does not appear we have\nseen the paper on this one either .\nthank you ,\nmelissa',ham
'Subject: important - to all domestic employees who participate in the enron\ncorp savings plan\nif you are a participant in the enron corp . savings plan , please read this very important message .\nwe understand that you are concerned about the timing of the move to a new savings plan administrator and the restricted access to your investment funds during the upcoming transition period scheduled to take place beginning at 3 : 00 pm cst on october 26 and ending at 8 : 00 am cst on november 20 .\nwe have been working with hewitt and northern trust since july . we understand your concerns and are committed to making this transition period as short as possible without jeopardizing the reconciliation of both the plan in total or your account in particular .\nremember that the enron corp . savings plan is an investment vehicle for your long - term financial goals . the enron plan will continue to offer a variety of investment opportunities with different levels of risk .\nas always , we advise you to review your overall investment strategy and carefully weigh the potential earnings of each investment choice against its risk before making investment decisions that are aligned with your long - term financial plans and your risk tolerance .\nfor that reason , it is critical that all trades among your investment funds be completed by 3 : 00 pm cst friday , october 26 before the transition period begins .',ham
