'Subject: cleburne ua 4 11 / 00\ndarren :\ni am working with jim pond to clean up the ua 4 that has been booked to cleburne since the beginning of the deal . we are starting with november 2000 . gas accounting has booked 21 , 309 mmbtu as ua 4 for november , which is related to deal 502861 on the texas desk . it looks like we took some of the gas we purchased from williams ( deal 384237 ) on the cleburne desk and moved it to ena \' s transport contract with deal 502861 . the print screen below shows the deal from zone transport to ena - texas . i think we need a deal from cleburne to zone transport to complete to deal path and clean up the ua 4 . can you review the deals for november and let me know what you think ? jim says there is ua 4 every month of this deal and this may be the reason . i will have to check each month .\nthanks ,\nmegan\n',ham
'Subject: sitara / cpr availability\nto all sitara users :\nthe sitara system will be brought down early this evening ( aug 11 th - 9 pm\ncentral time )\nto change the event transmission software to tibco . this software is used to\nsend data change events to\nsitara applications that are using portfolios ( position manager , deal ticker ,\nfacility assignment , deal manager ) .\nsignificant changes :\nnew deal level fees : transport reimbursement , demand reimbursement , transport\nreimbursement\nnew required field for storage service deal type : physical , synthetic\nadded help file for on - line user guide ( still being edited for content )\nadditional live link buttons to service deals ( for future use )\nadditional warnings and hints for primary and secondary service deals\nimproved audit for deleted data and d 2 d deals\nchanged price warning to $ 9 . 01 ( from $ 5 . 01 )\ncontract auto attaching matrix changed to exclude single transaction\ncontracts for on - line deals\nadded gst exempt flag to agency\nchanged default date for new efp to begin next month\nif you experience any problems with the release , please call the sitara\nhotline .\ncpr will be available during the outage .\nsitara will be available early saturday morning .\nplease call the sitara hotline ( ( 713 ) - 853 - 7049 ) if you have any questions or\nconcerns .',ham
